        {
          "duration": {
            "from": 343.4,
            "to": 353.4
          },
          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A patient with HIV has a CD4 count of 80 cells/µL. Which of the following opport</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A patient with HIV has a CD4 count of 80 cells/µL. Which of the following opportunistic infections is this patient specifically at risk for that would NOT typically occur at a CD4 count of 250?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Pulmonary tuberculosis</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Tuberculosis can strike at any CD4 level. It is not restricted to severely immunosuppressed patients and would be expected at CD4 of 250 as well.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Oral candidiasis</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Oral candidiasis appears when CD4 drops below approximately 300, so a patient at 250 would already be at risk. It is not specific to severe immunosuppression below 100.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Herpes zoster</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Herpes zoster can emerge at moderately reduced CD4 counts between 200 and 500 and is not specific to severe immunosuppression below 100.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Cryptococcal meningitis</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Cryptococcal meningitis typically appears at CD4 counts below 100. At a CD4 of 250, the immune system is still strong enough to prevent this infection, making it a threshold-specific diagnosis.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Recall the CD4 threshold ladder: TB can occur at any CD4 level, oral candidiasis below 300, herpes zoster between 200–500, but cryptococcal meningitis requires severe immunosuppression below 100."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct. Cryptococcal meningitis is a CD4 <100 infection — the CD4 threshold ladder tells you which infections are biologically possible at each level of immunosuppression."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
                "enableRetry": true,
                "enableSolutionsButton": true,
                "enableCheckButton": true,
