          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A 28-year-old woman with HIV has been on ART for one year and has achieved a sus</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A 28-year-old woman with HIV has been on ART for one year and has achieved a sustained undetectable viral load. She asks whether she can still sexually transmit HIV to her husband. What is the most appropriate counselling response?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>She can still transmit HIV and must always use condoms</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>While condoms prevent other STIs, omitting the U=U message undermines the patient's motivation. Evidence shows a sustained undetectable viral load means zero risk of sexual transmission.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>With a sustained undetectable viral load, she cannot sexually transmit HIV — this reinforces why daily adherence matters</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. The Undetectable = Untransmittable (U=U) principle is evidence-based. Sharing it empowers the patient by linking daily adherence directly to protecting loved ones, transforming motivation from fear to purpose.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Transmission risk is reduced but not eliminated, so barrier methods remain essential</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>This contradicts the U=U evidence. A sustained undetectable viral load means the virus cannot be sexually transmitted. Providing inaccurate information erodes trust and weakens adherence motivation.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>She should not worry about transmission since she is already on treatment</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Being on treatment alone is insufficient — the critical condition is achieving and sustaining an undetectable viral load, which requires adherence above 95%. Dismissing the concern without specifying this condition is clinically inaccurate.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Recall the U=U principle: a patient with a sustained undetectable viral load cannot sexually transmit HIV. This evidence-based message is central to effective prevention counselling and adherence motivation."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done. U=U is a powerful counselling tool — it transforms the daily tablet from a reminder of illness into an act of protection for loved ones."
                }
              ],
